 The dossiers required when carrying out procedures for registration of establishment of limited right of limited use of the adjacent land plot after the issuance of the initial certificate are as follows:

1. Application form for registration of changes of land and properties on land using Form No. 09/DK;
2. The original of the issued certificate of one or all parties concerned;
3. Contract or written agreement on the limited right to use the adjacent land plot.

These regulations are prescribed in Clause 8 Article 9 of Circular No. 24/2014/TT-BTNMT on cadastral documents promulgated by the Minister of Natural Resources and Environment.

 Based on the provided rules, an international tour guide must meet at least one of the following criteria to be considered a fluent foreign language user:

a) Possessing a college degree or higher in a foreign language;
b) Having a college degree or higher according to the training program in a language of a foreign country;
c) Having a college degree in a country according to the training program of the official language of the host country;
d) Have a foreign language certificate of level 4 or higher according to the 6-level foreign language competency framework for Vietnam or a foreign Language Certificate of satisfactory proficiency specified in Appendix I of this Circular issued by a competent authority.

Therefore, an international tour guide must have a college degree or higher in a foreign language or an equivalent foreign language certificate. However, it is not strictly necessary for the degree to be in foreign language specifically, as options b) and c) suggest that a degree in any field from a foreign institution or a degree in the host country's official language would also be acceptable.
